From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:25:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Pi-Bolt: ahead-of-time compiled executables

Bun's changes for Pi-Bolt's executables, on Linux x86-64 and macOS ARM64:

- Executables with a prebuilt heap and a code image, made by `bun build --compile` and mapped from the
  executable when it starts (bundler, StandaloneModuleGraph, ZigSourceProvider).
- Builtin modules imported in the order Node evaluates them; the names of a builtin module required in
  a wrapper read once, ahead of the wrapper's dependencies.
- Stack traces and crash reports of ahead-of-time code: no CodeBlocks made to read a frame, crash
  reports not uploaded unasked. The default Error.prepareStackTrace takes any object.
- Memory: garbage collection markers for the prebuilt heap, the allocator's idle sweep every 250 ms,
  static strings not reference counted from Rust; on macOS a starting heap budget that fits the
  prebuilt heap, and a collection every 5 seconds while the program waits.
- fetch: an idle connection waits in the keep-alive pool for 4 seconds, or as long as the server says.
- macOS: the prebuilt heap and code image mapped from the __BUN section, with the executable where it
  was linked to be; SharedArrayBuffer with the JIT off; a terminal reopened by its own device, which
  kqueue can watch; the programs an executable starts are started by Pi-Bolt's launcher helper.
